# The minimal law fell to 24.6 (#29), so darkness and trail are load-bearing, and the best structure is the knowledge-priced wave with its helpers. The one remaining unpriced thing in it is a SEEN wall: every wall cell passes the wave by its own taught leak, alike for rock and door; door contrast (#19) gave the best holdout (31.2) on the older base. Here walls are priced by their door contrast inside #23 (map completion + unknown-ground price), and darkness no longer counts guessed-wall cells as unexplored, so the whole map is priced by what the agent knows: seen floor cheap, unknown dearer, guessed wall dearer still, rock nearly shut, doors open.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel bad
channel here
channel leak
channel value
channel dark
channel guess
channel door
channel injection
channel wave
channel trail

rule track:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.97 * trail)

rule darkness:
  when 1
  set dark = 0.5 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid) * (1 - guess) + 0.5 * avg8(dark)

rule complete:
  when 1
  set guess = (1 - free) * (1 - solid) * max(shift(solid, 1, 0) * shift(solid, -1, 0), shift(solid, 0, 1) * shift(solid, 0, -1), 0.6 * shift(solid, 1, 0) * shift(solid, 2, 0), 0.6 * shift(solid, -1, 0) * shift(solid, -2, 0), 0.6 * shift(solid, 0, 1) * shift(solid, 0, 2), 0.6 * shift(solid, 0, -1) * shift(solid, 0, -2))

# a wall cell whose taught leak exceeds the walls around it stands out as a door
rule doorness:
  when 1
  set door = clamp(leak + 2.0 * (leak - sum8(solid * leak) / (sum8(solid) + 0.01)) * min(1, 0.5 * sum8(solid)), 0, 1)

rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(where(scent + thing < 0.05, 0, source), thing * (1 - bad), where(scent + thing < 0.05, source, 0) * (0.3 + 2.0 * dark) * (1 - guess)) / (1 + 0.5 * sum8(solid))

# the whole map priced by knowledge: unknown ground costs, guessed wall passes half, a seen wall passes by its door contrast
rule plan:
  when 1
  set wave = max(injection, (1 - 0.08 * (1 - free)) * max(0.94 * max4(wave), 0.916214 * max8(wave))) * (1 - solid * (1 - door)) * (1 - 0.5 * guess)

rule read:
  when 1
  set value = wave * (1 - 0.4 * trail)
